[Unit]
Description=Bunny Shell user session
Documentation=file:///usr/share/doc/bunny-os/BUNNY_SHELL.md
Wants=bunny-companion.service bunny-shell-status.service bunny-search-index.timer
After=graphical-session-pre.target
PartOf=graphical-session.target
# StopWhenUnneeded is deliberately absent. The target is started explicitly by
# the session wrapper (shell/session/bunny-shell-session.py) and referenced by
# nothing durable, so with StopWhenUnneeded=yes systemd reaped it the moment its
# start job completed — every recorded boot shows "Reached bunny-shell.target"
# followed the same second by "Stopped", taking bunny-shell-status.service and
# bunny-search-index.timer down with it (they are Wanted= here). Logout teardown
# is already guaranteed by PartOf= above; a stop must come only from the
# session ending, never from the target having no remaining referrers.
